---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Andi Monari — Building useful software"
  description="Andi Monari builds practical, AI-enabled products informed by a background in software engineering, strategy, and operations. Explore Roundwise and CambridgeLocals."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="intro-title">
      <div class="wrap hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="kicker"><span class="kicker-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span> Andi Monari <span class="kicker-sep">/</span> Cambridge, UK</p>
          <h1 id="intro-title">Ideas into<br /><em>useful software.</em></h1>
          <p class="hero-lede">
            I build practical products with AI, guided by a simple question:
            <strong>what would make this easier for a real person?</strong>
          </p>
          <p class="hero-support">
            I started in software engineering, spent the next chapter in strategy and operations,
            and came back to hands-on building in 2025. That mix helps me find the problem worth solving before reaching for the tools.
          </p>
          <div class="cta-row">
            <a href="#projects" class="btn primary btn--lg">Explore the work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a href="https://github.com/andimonari" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link">Find me on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="hero-aside" aria-label="A path from engineering to product building">
          <div class="aside-top"><span>THE PATH HERE</span><span>2002 → NOW</span></div>
          <ol class="path-list">
            <li><span class="path-year">2002</span><div><strong>Software engineering</strong><span>Started out on HP-UX systems.</span></div></li>
            <li><span class="path-year">2008</span><div><strong>Strategy & operations</strong><span>Learned how organisations work and where they get stuck.</span></div></li>
            <li><span class="path-year">2025</span><div><strong>Back to building</strong><span>Making focused products with modern AI tools.</span></div></li>
          </ol>
          <p class="aside-note">“The bottleneck is product thinking — knowing what to build and why.”</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <div class="wrap hero-index" aria-hidden="true"><span>01 / INTRODUCTION</span><span>SCROLL TO EXPLORE ↓</span></div>
    </section>

    <section id="projects" class="section projects-section" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="section-intro">
          <div><p class="kicker">01 / SELECTED WORK</p><h2 id="projects-title">Built around<br /><em>real problems.</em></h2></div>
          <p>The best technology gets out of the way. These projects begin with something people actually need to do.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="project-list">
          <article class="project-card">
            <div class="project-content">
              <div class="project-overline"><span>01 / INTERVIEW PRACTICE</span><span class="status status-building"><i aria-hidden="true"></i> IN PROGRESS</span></div>
              <h3>Roundwise</h3>
              <p class="project-tagline">Practice the interview before it counts.</p>
              <p class="project-description">A mock interview platform that uses a candidate’s CV to shape a timed, spoken interview with an AI panel. Afterwards, it returns scored feedback grounded in the conversation.</p>
              <div class="project-bottom">
                <div class="project-tags" aria-label="Technologies"><span>Next.js</span><span>Voice AI</span><span>Fastify</span></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="project-art roundwise-art" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="art-label">ROUNDWISE / PRACTICE ROOM</div>
              <div class="roundwise-orbit">
                <span class="orbit-ring orbit-ring--outer"></span>
                <span class="orbit-ring orbit-ring--inner"></span>
                <span class="orbit-core">RW</span>
                <span class="orbit-node orbit-node--one"></span>
                <span class="orbit-node orbit-node--two"></span>
                <span class="orbit-node orbit-node--three"></span>
              </div>
              <div class="roundwise-caption"><span>Practice. Reflect. Improve.</span><small>01 / 02 / 03</small></div>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="project-card">
            <div class="project-content">
              <div class="project-overline"><span>02 / LOCAL DISCOVERY</span><span class="status status-building"><i aria-hidden="true"></i> IN PROGRESS</span></div>
              <h3>CambridgeLocals</h3>
              <p class="project-tagline">A better welcome to a new city.</p>
              <p class="project-description">A practical guide for people moving to Cambridge, bringing neighbourhoods, schools, services, and community groups together in one place.</p>
              <div class="project-bottom">
                <div class="project-tags" aria-label="Technologies"><span>Next.js</span><span>TypeScript</span><span>Prisma</span></div>
                <div class="project-links"><a href="https://github.com/andimonari/cambridgelocals" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="project-art city-art" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="art-label">CAMBRIDGE / UK</div>
              <div class="map-lines"><span class="map-route"></span><span class="map-pin pin-one"></span><span class="map-pin pin-two"></span><span class="map-pin pin-three"></span></div>
              <div class="city-caption"><span>Find your place.</span><small>52.1951° N&nbsp; 0.1313° E</small></div>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="approach" class="section notes-section" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
      <div class="wrap notes-grid">
        <div class="notes-main">
          <p class="kicker">02 / APPROACH</p>
          <h2 id="approach-title">Useful beats clever.</h2>
          <div class="approach-copy">
            <p>The hard part is deciding what to build. I start with the real task someone faces, remove avoidable friction, and use modern AI tools to turn that understanding into a working product.</p>
            <p>Roundwise helps people prepare for interviews by practising aloud and seeing grounded feedback. CambridgeLocals brings scattered local information together for people finding their feet in a new city. Different problems, same starting point: make the next step easier.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="elsewhere" class="contact-panel">
          <p class="kicker">03 / ELSEWHERE</p>
          <h2>The work<br />continues.</h2>
          <p>More projects, experiments, and source code live on my GitHub profile.</p>
          <a href="https://github.com/andimonari" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="contact-link">Explore GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
